# PostCribe Project Rules

## Tech Stack
- **Runtime & Package Manager**: Bun (version 1.2.13+)
- **Language**: TypeScript (version 5.8.2+)
- **Monorepo**: Turborepo with workspaces pattern
- **Node Version**: >= 18
- **Database**: Prisma ORM with PostgreSQL
- **Frontend**: Next.js 15 with React 19
- **Styling**: Tailwind CSS v4 with shadcn/ui components
- **Authentication**: Better-Auth with Google OAuth integration

## Project Structure

### Monorepo Layout
- `apps/` - Application packages
  - `api/` - Main backend API server
  - `cron-handler/` - Cron job processing service
  - `cron-sender/` - Cron job scheduling service  
  - `schedule-handler/` - Schedule management service
  - `web/` - Frontend Next.js application
- `packages/` - Shared packages
  - `ai/` - AI and LLM integration logic
  - `auth/` - Authentication utilities and Better-Auth configuration
  - `db/` - Database schema and migrations
  - `linkedin/` - LinkedIn API integration
  - `x/` - Twitter/X API integration
  - `mailer/` - Email sending utilities
  - `s3/` - AWS S3 file storage utilities
  - `shared/` - Common utilities and types
  - `template/` - Template processing
  - `logger/` - Logging utilities

### Key Configuration Files
- [package.json](mdc:package.json) - Root package configuration
- [turbo.json](mdc:turbo.json) - Turborepo task configuration
- [docker-compose.yml](mdc:docker-compose.yml) - Docker services setup

## Development Guidelines

### Documentation Research
- **ALWAYS** search Context7 MCP docs first for latest documentation
- Use short, optimized queries for vector search
- Search multiple times with different query variations for better results
- Only use web search if Context7 docs don't have the information

### Code Standards
- **TypeScript**: Use strict mode, properly type all variables and functions
- **Imports**: Use absolute imports with `@/` prefix where configured
- **Formatting**: Use Prettier with existing configuration
- **Linting**: Follow ESLint rules defined in packages
- **React**: Use React 19 features, hooks pattern, and functional components

### Database
- **ORM**: Prisma is used for database operations
- **Migrations**: Located in [packages/db/src/prisma/migrations/](mdc:packages/db/src/prisma/migrations)
- **Schema**: Main schema in packages/db/src/prisma/

### API Development
- **Structure**: Controllers, middlewares, and routers in apps/api/src/
- **Platform Controllers**: Located in [apps/api/src/controllers/platform-login-controllers/](mdc:apps/api/src/controllers/platform-login-controllers)
- **Post Controllers**: Located in [apps/api/src/controllers/post-controllers/](mdc:apps/api/src/controllers/post-controllers)

### Frontend Development
- **Location**: All frontend code in [apps/web/](mdc:apps/web)
- **Framework**: Next.js 15 with App Router pattern
- **Port**: Development server runs on port 3001 (`bun dev`)
- **Components**: Use shadcn/ui components from [apps/web/src/components/ui/](mdc:apps/web/src/components/ui)
- **Pages**: App router structure in [apps/web/src/app/](mdc:apps/web/src/app)
- **Config**: Environment configuration in [apps/web/src/config.ts](mdc:apps/web/src/config.ts)
- **Guidelines**: 
  - UI/UX patterns: [frontend-ui-guidelines.mdc](mdc:.cursor/rules/frontend-ui-guidelines.mdc)
  - Current implementation: [web-app-implementation.mdc](mdc:.cursor/rules/web-app-implementation.mdc)

#### Current Frontend Architecture
```
apps/web/src/
├── app/                           # Next.js 15 App Router
│   ├── (authorized)/             # Protected routes group
│   │   ├── dashboard/            # Main dashboard
│   │   ├── settings/             # User settings page
│   │   └── layout.tsx            # Auth wrapper layout
│   ├── signin/                   # Login page
│   ├── signup/                   # Registration page
│   ├── verify-email/             # Email verification
│   ├── globals.css               # Global styles with Tailwind v4
│   ├── layout.tsx                # Root layout with providers
│   └── page.tsx                  # Landing page
├── components/
│   ├── ui/                       # shadcn/ui components
│   │   ├── loaders/              # Loading components
│   │   │   ├── three-dot-loader.tsx
│   │   │   └── index.ts
│   │   ├── headings.tsx          # H1, H2, H3, Subtitle components
│   │   ├── login-checker.tsx     # Auth route protection
│   │   ├── resend-verification-email.tsx # Email verification UI
│   │   ├── timezone.tsx          # Timezone selection component
│   │   └── [other shadcn components]
│   └── providers/                # React context providers
│       ├── theme-provider.tsx    # Dark/light theme
│       └── providers.tsx         # Combined providers
├── lib/
│   ├── auth-client.ts            # Better-Auth client setup
│   ├── timezones.json            # Timezone data (1451 entries)
│   └── utils.ts                  # Utility functions (cn, etc.)
└── config.ts                     # Environment variables
```

#### Authentication System
- **Provider**: Better-Auth v1.2.8 with Google OAuth
- **Client**: [apps/web/src/lib/auth-client.ts](mdc:apps/web/src/lib/auth-client.ts)
- **Package**: [@repo/auth](mdc:packages/auth) workspace package
- **Route Protection**: [login-checker.tsx](mdc:apps/web/src/components/ui/login-checker.tsx)
- **Features**: Email/password signup, Google OAuth, email verification, timezone selection

#### Component Usage Priority
1. **Check existing components first** - Always look in `components/ui/` before creating new ones
2. **Use shadcn/ui directly** - Import components from `@/components/ui/`
3. **Reuse patterns** - Check `headings.tsx`, `loaders/`, `resend-verification-email.tsx` for examples
4. **Follow typing** - Use proper TypeScript interfaces and Better-Auth types

### Social Media Integration
- **LinkedIn**: Use utilities from packages/linkedin/
- **Twitter/X**: Use utilities from packages/x/
- **API Docs**: Reference [linkedin-api-client-docs.mdc](mdc:.cursor/rules/linkedin-api-client-docs.mdc) and [twitter-api-v2-docs.mdc](mdc:.cursor/rules/twitter-api-v2-docs.mdc)

## Build & Development Commands

### Available Scripts
- `bun dev` - Start development servers
- `bun build` - Build all packages
- `bun lint` - Run linting
- `bun format` - Format code with Prettier
- `bun check-types` - TypeScript type checking

### Web App Specific (apps/web)
- `bun dev` - Next.js dev server on port 3001 with Turbopack
- `bun build` - Production build
- `bun start` - Production server
- `bun lint` - ESLint validation

### Turborepo Tasks
- **Build**: Runs with dependency graph resolution
- **Dev**: Persistent, no cache for live development  
- **Lint**: Cascades through all packages
- **Check-types**: TypeScript validation across workspace

## File Naming Conventions
- **Components**: PascalCase (e.g., `UserProfile.tsx`)
- **Utilities**: camelCase (e.g., `formatDate.ts`)
- **Types**: PascalCase with `.types.ts` suffix
- **Constants**: UPPER_SNAKE_CASE in separate files
- **API Routes**: kebab-case for endpoints
- **Pages**: lowercase (e.g., `page.tsx`, `layout.tsx`)

## Environment & Deployment
- **Docker**: Use [docker-compose.yml](mdc:docker-compose.yml) for local development
- **Deployment**: Reference [DEPLOYMENT.md](mdc:DEPLOYMENT.md) for deployment instructions
- **Environment**: Configure environment variables per service
- **Frontend URLs**: 
  - CLIENT_URL: `http://localhost:3001` (dev)
  - API_URL: `http://localhost:30011` (dev)
  - BETTER_AUTH_URL: `http://localhost:3000/v1/auth` (dev)

## AI & LLM Integration
- **Package**: All AI logic in packages/ai/
- **Functions**: AI functions in [packages/ai/src/functions/](mdc:packages/ai/src/functions)
- **Graphs**: AI workflows in [packages/ai/src/graphs/](mdc:packages/ai/src/graphs)
- **Tools**: AI tools in [packages/ai/src/tools/](mdc:packages/ai/src/tools)

